<FeatureLayout
  title="Import & Reverse Engineer PostgreSQL Schemas"
  description="Import PostgreSQL schemas from MicroOLAP PDD, DbSchema DBS, Toad DM2, plain SQL, or a live database via pg_catalog introspection. One command to convert any source to .pgd."
  subtitle="Coming from another tool? Connect to a live database? One command converts any source into a PgDesigner project."
>

<h2>Five sources, one output</h2>

<p>PgDesigner reads schemas from five different sources and converts them into its native <code>.pgd</code> format — tables, columns, indexes, foreign keys, constraints, enums, domains, sequences, views, functions, triggers, and comments. The SQL path is round-trip tested on real databases: SQL → <code>.pgd</code> → DDL → PostgreSQL → <code>pg_dump</code> → <code>.pgd</code> with zero diff.</p>

<div class="not-prose grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-6 mb-8">
  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-1">MicroOLAP Database Designer</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted"><code>.pdd</code> — native XML format. MicroOLAP hasn't been updated since 2021, but your projects aren't lost.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-1">DbSchema</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted"><code>.dbs</code> — XML-based schema files from DbSchema.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-1">Toad Data Modeler</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted"><code>.dm2</code> — XML format from Quest Toad Data Modeler.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-1">Plain SQL / pg_dump</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted"><code>.sql</code> — any PostgreSQL DDL file, including <code>pg_dump</code> output. Parsed with the real PG17 parser (via WebAssembly).</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Reverse engineering from a live database</h2>

<div class="not-prose -mx-4 sm:mx-0 mt-2 mb-8">
  <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border-default shadow-xl img-zoom">
    <picture class="hidden dark:block">
      <source srcset="/images/blog/v002-dsn-dark.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img src="/images/blog/v002-dsn-dark.png" alt="PgDesigner DSN Introspection dialog connecting to PostgreSQL and showing schemas in dark theme" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="1024" class="w-full" />
    </picture>
    <picture class="block dark:hidden">
      <source srcset="/images/blog/v002-dsn-light.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img src="/images/blog/v002-dsn-light.png" alt="PgDesigner DSN Introspection dialog connecting to PostgreSQL and showing schemas in light theme" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="1024" class="w-full" />
    </picture>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Pass a PostgreSQL connection string instead of a file path. PgDesigner connects to your database and introspects the schema via <code>pg_catalog</code> queries:</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd "postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb"
pgdesigner convert -full -schema public,billing -o project.pgd "postgres://localhost/mydb"</code></pre>

<p>Always extracted:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Tables and columns (types, defaults, identity, nullable, storage, compression, comments)</li>
  <li>Indexes (btree, hash, gin, gist, brin — with INCLUDE columns)</li>
  <li>Primary keys, foreign keys, UNIQUE, CHECK, EXCLUDE constraints</li>
  <li>Sequences</li>
  <li>Partitions (RANGE, LIST, HASH — with bounds)</li>
</ul>

<p>Add <code>-full</code> for extensions, enums, domains, views, materialized views (with their indexes), functions, and triggers. <code>-schema</code> limits introspection to the listed schemas.</p>

<p>In the visual editor, <strong>File → Open… → PostgreSQL</strong> connects first and shows a preview of what's there — then you pick the schemas, individual tables, and object categories (views, functions, triggers, enums, domains, sequences, extensions) to import.</p>

<h2>CLI</h2>

<pre><code>pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd schema.pdd
pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd schema.dbs
pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd schema.dm2
pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd schema.sql
pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd "postgres://localhost:5432/mydb"</code></pre>

<p>The <code>-o</code> flag sets the output file. Without it, PgDesigner uses the input filename with a <code>.pgd</code> extension.</p>

<h2>Migrating from MicroOLAP?</h2>

<p>MicroOLAP Database Designer for PostgreSQL hasn't been updated since July 2021. If you have <code>.pdd</code> project files, PgDesigner reads them natively — no intermediate steps. Convert and open in the visual editor in seconds:</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner convert -o myproject.pgd myproject.pdd
pgdesigner myproject.pgd</code></pre>

